# Moved from bootstrap/examples/layout-self-unused.moss. Verdicts below credited to the
# oracle are the old Rocq oracle's (moss_m2, removed when moss-ref replaced
# it), so they are historical; the suite checks the current verdicts.
# D58 (AUDIT-CHANGES #90): the check is on definitions. `LCell` contains
# itself, and nothing uses it.
# Verdicts: Audit rejects (FiniteLayouts). Before #90 the oracle and native
# checked layouts only where a type is used, and accepted this program;
# with #90's changes both reject it ("`LCell` contains itself, so it has no
# finite layout (D58)"; "this type has no finite runtime layout").
tag LNil;
tag LCell { head: (), tail: LNil | LCell };
fn main() {}
